    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d342">

                <pb facs="0540" n="426" xml:id="pg426"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.48/96: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the High Commissioner
                        at Constantinople</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-09-19T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 19,
                                1922—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>133. Department’s 122 September 15, 5 p.m.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d342-f1"/> and
                    131 September 19, 10 a.m.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d342-f2"/></p>
                <p>Press reports today indicate that only relief work being carried on in Smyrna is
                    by Near East Relief, Red Cross and your destroyers and that only foreign forces
                    ashore are American sailors. Please confirm this report and advise Department
                    immediately (1) what relief stores are available for distribution if funds were
                    forthcoming; (2) whether any provision could be made for caring for refugees in
                    Greece or the Aegean Islands if facilities for evacuation were at hand.</p>
                <p>Advise Department frankly and fully of facilities which you need in order that
                    this Government may do its full part and more if necessary in helping to meet
                    tragic situation at Smyrna as described by press reports received yesterday and
                    today.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
